    • Briefly summarize The Gaming Room client and their software requirements. Who was the client? What type of software did they want you to design?
      
      The client was The Gaming Room, and they wanted to turn their Android mobile game, Draw It or Lose It, into a cross-platform game. 
      They needed a system design that allows users on Windows, Mac, Linux, and iOS to connect over the internet and play together at the same time.

    • What did you do particularly well in developing this documentation?
      
      Already having a strong grasp on the different operating system and how they work, I found it easy to translate my technical
      computer science knowledge into well worded sentences need for the Software Design Document. Being able to convey highly technical ideas
      to The Gaming Rooms executives was an important process of software development process.
      
    • What about the process of working through a design document did you find helpful when developing the code?
      
      Planning the three-tier architecture beforehand made coding much easier because the Client, Application, and Data tiers were already mapped out.
      Knowing exactly how games, teams, and players connected saved time and stopped any confusion when writing the Java code.
      
    • If you could choose one part of your work on these documents to revise, what would you pick? How would you improve it?
      
      I felt that I could have provided more context to each section in the Evaluation matrix where I compared different aspects of all 
      four operating platforms. I think that small size of each box in the matrix limited me to only a couple of sentences worth of test, 
      but each sections could have had a paragraph or two providing even more detail.
      
    • How did you interpret the user’s needs and implement them into your software design? 
      why is it so important to consider the user’s needs when designing?
      
      When designing software for a company, their user’s needs are critical considerations when developing the code. The whole point of this 
      business transaction is to deliver a product that the customer strongly desires which will bring The Gaming Room higher profits. 
      The technical requirements given to us by The Gaming Room helped me interpret the user’s needs: each team will have multiple players, 
      teams must be able to choose their own custom team name etc. In another course I recently took, I learned about implementing User Stories 
      into the software development process and think they would be have been very helpful for this project.
      
    • How did you approach designing software? What techniques or strategies would you use in the future to analyze and design a similar software application?
      
      I approached the design by comparing different operating systems to find the most stable, cost-effective setup, 
      which led to choosing a Linux server and a MySQL database. In the future, I would use network simulation tools 
      early on to test how well the servers handle different platforms before writing the final plan.
